      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Greenup''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]], at the [[confluence]] of the [[Ohio River|Ohio]] and [[Little Sandy River (Kentucky)|Little Sandy]] Rivers.  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,198.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Greenup County, Kentucky|Greenup County]]{{GR|6}}.  Greenup is named in honor of [[Christopher Greenup]].

Greenup is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-Greenup.PNG|right|Location of Greenup, Kentucky]]
Greenup is located at 38&amp;deg;34'25&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;50'1&quot; West (38.573503, -82.833549){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.0 km&amp;sup2; (0.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 34.17% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,198 people, 478 households, and 321 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 585.5/km&amp;sup2; (1,523.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 526 housing units at an average density of 257.1/km&amp;sup2; (668.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 90.07% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 8.85% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.25% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.17% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.17% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.50% from two or more races.  0.75% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 478 households out of which 24.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.8% are non-families. 31.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.27 and the average family size is 2.83.

In the city the population is spread out with 18.5% under the age of 18, 10.2% from 18 to 24, 30.1% from 25 to 44, 22.8% from 45 to 64, and 18.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 96.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $33,158, and the median income for a family is $41,548. Males have a median income of $33,750 versus $23,036 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,926.  10.7% of the population and 6.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.7% of those under the age of 18 and 12.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==See also==
*[[List of cities and towns along the Ohio River]]

== External links ==
