      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Raceland''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]], along the [[Ohio River]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 2,355.

Raceland is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-Raceland.PNG|right|Location of Raceland, Kentucky]]
Raceland is located at 38&amp;deg;32'13&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;43'52&quot; West (38.537003, -82.731137){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 5.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  5.7 km&amp;sup2; (2.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,355 people, 935 households, and 707 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 413.3/km&amp;sup2; (1,068.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,002 housing units at an average density of 175.9/km&amp;sup2; (454.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 99.07% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.47% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.04% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.04% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.38% from two or more races.  0.34% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 935 households out of which 33.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 59.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.3% are non-families. 21.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 2.92.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.5% under the age of 18, 8.2% from 18 to 24, 29.5% from 25 to 44, 24.7% from 45 to 64, and 13.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $31,500, and the median income for a family is $37,955. Males have a median income of $38,906 versus $19,189 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,537.  13.6% of the population and 10.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 18.6% of those under the age of 18 and 6.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
The city sits within the [http://www.raceland.k12.ky.us/ Raceland-Worthington Independent School District], which also includes the neighboring city of [[Worthington, Kentucky|Worthington]]. Two schools, Campbell Elementary School and Raceland-Worthington High School, are located in the city.

