      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Russell''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]], along the [[Ohio River]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,645.

Russell is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-Russell.PNG|right|Location of Russell, Kentucky]]
Russell is located at 38&amp;deg;31'5&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;41'52&quot; West (38.518176, -82.697680){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.4 km&amp;sup2; (4.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 3,645 people, 1,428 households, and 1,106 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 351.8/km&amp;sup2; (910.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,584 housing units at an average density of 152.9/km&amp;sup2; (395.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.49% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.71% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.03% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 2.14% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.22% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.41% from two or more races.  0.82% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,428 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 67.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.5% are non-families. 20.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.50 and the average family size is 2.88.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.7% under the age of 18, 7.1% from 18 to 24, 25.1% from 25 to 44, 29.7% from 45 to 64, and 16.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $53,869, and the median income for a family is $62,018. Males have a median income of $50,306 versus $30,494 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $29,453.  6.0% of the population and 4.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 11.1% of those under the age of 18 and 2.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
Russell is located within the [http://www.russell-ind.k12.ky.us/ Russell Independent School District], which it shares with its neighbors, [[Flatwoods, Kentucky|Flatwoods]] and [[Bellefonte, Kentucky|Bellefonte]]. The main campus, which includes Russell High School, Russell Middle School, Russell Primary School and the Russell Area Technology Center, sit on the Russell/Flatwoods city line (All of the school's mailing addresses are Russell but they receive primary police and fire protection from Flatwoods).  In addition, the district's central office is located in downtown Russell.

==See also==
*[[List of cities and towns along the Ohio River]]

== External links ==
*[http://www.olbh.com Our Lady of Bellefonte Hospital] is located in Russell.
