      <text xml:space="preserve">'''South Shore''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,226.  It is located along the [[Ohio River]] across from [[Portsmouth, Ohio]]. 

South Shore is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-SouthShore.PNG|right|Location of South Shore, Kentucky]]
South Shore is located at 38&amp;deg;43'18&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;57'49&quot; West (38.721577, -82.963606){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 2.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.7 km&amp;sup2; (0.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.4 km&amp;sup2; (0.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 20.00% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,226 people, 539 households, and 335 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 739.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,916.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 605 housing units at an average density of 365.0/km&amp;sup2; (945.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.55% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.16% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.57% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.08% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.24% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.39% from two or more races.  0.24% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 539 households out of which 29.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 44.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 15.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 37.7% are non-families. 34.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.17 and the average family size is 2.80.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.2% under the age of 18, 8.7% from 18 to 24, 24.9% from 25 to 44, 21.2% from 45 to 64, and 21.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 74.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 70.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $18,214, and the median income for a family is $25,197. Males have a median income of $23,036 versus $20,833 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $12,161.  25.7% of the population and 22.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 35.3% of those under the age of 18 and 16.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

