      <comment>/* Ashland Regional Airport */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Worthington''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]], along the [[Ohio River]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,673.

Worthington is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 

== Ashland Regional Airport ==
[[Image:IM001069.JPG|thumb|right|A Russian MiG takes off from Ashland Regional Airport]]
Located in Worthington, and named for nearby [[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], the '''[http://www.ashlandregionalairport.com Ashland Regional Airport]''' was once used extensively by the oil manufacturing company [[Ashland Inc.]] before the company's corporate headquaters was moved from [[Russell, Kentucky|Russell]] to [[Covington, Kentucky|Covington]]. Currently, the airport serves local charter and private aircraft. Recently, community events, such as car and air shows, have also taken place at the airport.

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-Worthington.PNG|right|Location of Worthington, Kentucky]]
Worthington is located at 38&amp;deg;33'2&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;44'5&quot; West (38.550616, -82.734694){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.0 km&amp;sup2; (1.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.50% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,673 people, 663 households, and 519 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 552.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,427.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 698 housing units at an average density of 230.3/km&amp;sup2; (595.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.74% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.06% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.06% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.36% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.78% from two or more races.  0.78% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 663 households out of which 31.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 62.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 21.6% are non-families. 19.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.3% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 26.7% from 25 to 44, 27.4% from 45 to 64, and 15.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $34,875, and the median income for a family is $39,737. Males have a median income of $35,324 versus $19,643 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $19,239.  9.3% of the population and 7.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 12.8% of those under the age of 18 and 6.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Education==
The city sits within the [http://www.raceland.k12.ky.us Raceland-Worthington Independent School District], which also includes the neighboring city of [[Raceland, Kentucky|Raceland]]. One school, Worthington Elementary School, is located in the city.

