      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wurtland''' is a city located in [[Greenup County, Kentucky]], along the [[Ohio River]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,049. Wurtland is a part of the [[Huntington, West Virginia|Huntington]]-[[Ashland, Kentucky|Ashland]], [[West Virginia|WV]]-[[Kentucky|KY]]-[[Ohio|OH]], [[Metropolitan Statistical Area]] (MSA). As of the 2000 census, the MSA had a population of 288,649. 


The northern terminus of the [[KY 67|Industrial Parkway]] ([[KY 67]]) ends at [[US 23]] at Wurtland. This highway serves to connect Wurtland and the surrounding towns of [[Greenup, Kentucky|Greenup]] and [[Flatwoods, Kentucky|Flatwoods]] to the [[EastPark, Kentucky|EastPark]] industrial park and [[Interstate 64]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-Wurtland.PNG|right|Location of Wurtland, Kentucky]]
