== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 996 people, 405 households, and 287 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 61.1/km&amp;sup2; (158.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 448 housing units at an average density of 27.5/km&amp;sup2; (71.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 97.29% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.51% from two or more races.  1.20% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 405 households out of which 33.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 55.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.9% are non-families. 26.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.46 and the average family size is 2.98.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 26.1% under the age of 18, 7.4% from 18 to 24, 27.4% from 25 to 44, 24.1% from 45 to 64, and 15.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 81.3 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $19,650, and the median income for a family is $23,083. Males have a median income of $30,417 versus $18,906 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $9,357.  36.7% of the population and 32.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 44.3% of those under the age of 18 and 15.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

