      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Wallins Creek''' is a city located in [[Harlan County, Kentucky]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 257.

== Geography ==
[[Image:KYMap-doton-WallinsCreek.PNG|right|Location of Wallins Creek, Kentucky]]
Wallins Creek is located at 36&amp;deg;49'41&quot; North, 83&amp;deg;24'52&quot; West (36.828036, -83.414449){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 1.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (0.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  1.0 km&amp;sup2; (0.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 257 people, 112 households, and 73 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 254.4/km&amp;sup2; (657.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 126 housing units at an average density of 124.7/km&amp;sup2; (322.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.28% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.39% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.33% from two or more races.  0.00% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 112 households out of which 25.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 47.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 16.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.8% are non-families. 29.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.7% under the age of 18, 3.5% from 18 to 24, 26.8% from 25 to 44, 28.8% from 45 to 64, and 17.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $11,083, and the median income for a family is $16,563. Males have a median income of $17,500 versus $20,625 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $8,151.  44.2% of the population and 47.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 46.9% of those under the age of 18 and 14.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== History ==

Wallins Creek began life as a [[coal]]mining town; the mine was owned by the Wallins Creek Coal Corporation.  The Wallins Creek [[Baptist church]] was established in 1855 with 30 members.

Wallins Creek is said to be [[ghost|haunted]] by an old coal miner who died in an explosion and who walks alongside the roadside to his former home.

