      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Buechel''' is a former [[census-designated place]] located in [[Jefferson County, Kentucky]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 7,272. In [[2003]], The area was [[annexed]] to the city of [[Louisville, Kentucky|Louisville]] due to a merger between the city and Jefferson County's [[unincorporated|unincorporated communities]]. Buechel is now a [[neighborhood]] within the city limits of [[Louisville, Kentucky|Louisville]].


== Geography ==
Buechel is located at 38&amp;deg;11'28&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;38'33&quot; West (38.191169, -85.642393){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 6.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.5 km&amp;sup2; (2.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of it is covered by water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,272 people, 3,320 households, and 1,792 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 1,114.2/km&amp;sup2; (2,890.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 3,505 housing units at an average density of 537.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,393.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 76.43% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 17.86% [[African American (U.S. Census)|Black]] or [[Race (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.23% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.42% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.31% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.73% from two or more races.  4.07% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 3,320 households out of which 25.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 36.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 46.0% are non-families. 39.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.15 and the average family size is 2.88.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 22.4% under the age of 18, 9.4% from 18 to 24, 31.8% from 25 to 44, 19.7% from 45 to 64, and 16.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 87.0 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $35,650, and the median income for a family is $43,375. Males have a median income of $31,376 versus $24,604 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $19,426.  7.8% of the population and 5.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 9.7% of those under the age of 18 and 8.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

